      "hints": [
        "A repeated linear factor requires the form \\(\\frac{A}{1-x}+\\frac{B}{2+3x}+\\frac{C}{(2+3x)^2}\\).",
        "Multiply through by \\((1-x)(2+3x)^2\\) to create a polynomial identity.",
        "Substitute \\(x=1\\) and \\(x=-2/3\\) to isolate two coefficients, then use a convenient third value or compare coefficients to find the last one."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "State or imply the form $A/(1-x)+B/(2+3x)+C/(2+3x)^2$",
        "Use a correct method for finding a coefficient",
        "Obtain one of $A=1$, $B=-1$, $C=6$",
        "Obtain a second value",
        "Obtain the third value",
        "$f(x)=\\frac{1}{1-x}-\\frac{1}{2+3x}+\\frac{6}{(2+3x)^2}$."
      ],
